    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Periods can now be closed. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec (the main \"close period\" test and scenarios 1\u20133).\n\n**Stored data:** a new migration, `V14__period_closed.sql`, adds a `closed` flag and a `closed_total` to each period.\n\n**Server:**\n- **Closing:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/periods/{name}/close`, works out the period's due-total, stores it with the period and writes `PERIOD_CLOSED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 period=<name> total=<due-total>` to the audit file. The total counts only OPEN and SETTLED claims dated in the period. Each claim's figure is worked out the same way the person rollups already do it, so it matches what the screen showed before closing. Closing a period that is already closed, or one that doesn't exist, is refused and writes nothing.\n- **Claim checks:** a new step in each claim endpoint refuses any claim dated inside a closed period:\n  - **Adding:** refused if the claim's date falls in a closed period. With no date given, the sheet's today is used.\n  - **Editing:** refused if the claim is already in a closed period, or if the new date would move it into one.\n  - **Open, settle, void:** refused if the claim is in a closed period.\n\n  Each check runs before anything is written, so a refused change leaves the store and the audit file unchanged.\n\n**Front end:** each period row now shows `period-closed` (yes/no) and has a `period-close` button and a `period-error` message. A closed period's `period-due-total` shows the stored total, so later rate changes don't alter it; an open period still works its total out live. The existing claim errors (`claim-form-error` and `claim-error`) show the refusals.\n\n**Limitations:** there is no way to reopen a closed period. The test helper mentions a `reopen` action, but this request doesn't ask for it.",
